"""Build a reviewed, additive curriculum migration; never connects to a database."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
rows = [
('A1','A day at the library','The library opens at nine. Ana goes there on Monday. She reads a book and studies with her friend.','Use the present simple for regular actions. With he or she, add -s: Ana reads. With I or they, use the base form: They read. Use at for clock times and on for days.','Ana ___ a book every Monday.','reads','read','reading','When does the library open?','At nine.','At noon.','At five.','When does Ana go to the library?','On Monday.','On Friday.','Every evening.','study with a friend','learn together','buy a book','close a building','Write three sentences about a place you visit. Say when you go, what you do, and who goes with you.','Use familiar words, a present-simple verb in each sentence, and at or on with an appropriate time.'),
('A2','Changing a travel plan','Sam usually takes the bus to work. Yesterday the road was closed, so he walked to the station instead. He arrived ten minutes late and called his manager. Tomorrow he will leave earlier.','Use the past simple for finished events: He walked yesterday. Irregular verbs change form: take becomes took. Use will plus a base verb for a future decision: He will leave earlier. Instead signals a replacement choice.','Yesterday Sam ___ to the station.','walked','walks','will walk','Why did Sam change his journey?','The road was closed.','He lost his ticket.','The station was closed.','What will Sam do tomorrow?','Leave earlier.','Call a taxi at noon.','Stay at home.','instead','in place of another choice','at the same time','without a reason','Write a message to a friend about a journey that went wrong. Explain what happened and what you will do differently next time.','Use past-simple verbs for the problem, so or because for a reason, and will for the next plan.'),
('B1','A repair workshop','Our neighbourhood has held a repair workshop every month since March. Last Saturday, volunteers repaired twelve appliances. Visitors say they have learned useful skills, although some repairs take longer than expected. The organisers plan to train more volunteers.','Use the present perfect for a situation continuing to now: has held workshops since March. Use past simple for a finished occasion: repaired twelve last Saturday. Although introduces a contrast without removing either fact.','The group ___ monthly workshops since March.','has held','held yesterday','is hold','What happened last Saturday?','Volunteers repaired twelve appliances.','The workshop permanently closed.','Twelve volunteers left.','Why train more volunteers?','To increase the workshop’s repair capacity.','To stop visitors learning.','To replace all appliances.','appliance','a machine used for a household task','a public speech','an outdoor path','Describe a useful community activity. Explain how long it has existed, mention one past event, and suggest an improvement.','Distinguish continuing experience from a finished event. Support your suggestion with a concrete reason and link ideas with because or although.'),
('B2','Testing a flexible schedule','A company piloted a four-day schedule for six months. Output remained stable, while staff reported lower stress. However, customers faced longer waits on Fridays. The director proposed staggered days off rather than closing the office on a single day.','Use a past passive when the action matters more than the agent: A schedule was piloted. While can contrast two outcomes. Rather than presents a preferred alternative. A balanced recommendation acknowledges evidence against it.','A four-day schedule ___ for six months.','was piloted','has piloting','was pilot','What trade-off did the pilot reveal?','Stable output and lower stress came with Friday delays.','All customers received faster replies.','Output stopped entirely.','Why stagger days off?','To retain coverage throughout the week.','To close every Friday.','To eliminate annual leave.','staggered','arranged at different times','cancelled without notice','identical for everyone','Recommend whether to extend the pilot. Use the reported outcomes, recognise a customer concern, and propose a practical safeguard.','State a clear recommendation, integrate both benefits and costs, and explain how the safeguard addresses the specific concern. Avoid claiming that six months proves a universal result.'),
('C1','Interpreting an urban study','Researchers found an association between access to green space and reported wellbeing. The observational study controlled for income, but could not rule out residential self-selection. Its authors cautioned that the findings warranted further investigation rather than a definitive causal claim.','Hedging calibrates a claim to evidence: may indicate and is consistent with preserve uncertainty. Having controlled for income does not mean having controlled for every confounder. Use concessive clauses to preserve this distinction: Although income was controlled for, self-selection remained possible.','The results ___ an association, without establishing causation.','suggest','prove beyond doubt','rule out','Which limitation remains?','People may choose neighbourhoods based on existing preferences.','Income was never considered.','No association was observed.','What would be a proportionate next step?','Investigate alternative explanations with additional research.','Declare that parks cure all illness.','Discard all observational research.','warranted','provided sufficient reason for','guaranteed the outcome of','made legally impossible','Write a short policy briefing interpreting the study. Distinguish its finding from a causal claim and recommend a proportionate response.','Accurately describe observational evidence, explain self-selection in plain language, and qualify the recommendation without becoming vague. Do not invent an effect size.'),
('C2','Designing accountable consultation','The council’s consultation attracted substantial participation, yet renters were underrepresented. Notwithstanding its procedural openness, the process risked conferring legitimacy on priorities shaped chiefly by homeowners. A revised approach would retain open submissions while commissioning targeted outreach, with independent scrutiny of whose views informed the final decision.','Concession can distinguish formal legitimacy from substantive representation. Notwithstanding means despite and takes a noun phrase. In formal inversion, a fronted negative expression moves the auxiliary before the subject: Rarely has participation alone guaranteed representation. Use such emphasis sparingly.','Rarely ___ representation on its own.','has participation guaranteed','participation has guaranteed','has guaranteed participation','What is the central criticism?','An open procedure can still underrepresent affected groups.','Participation was prohibited.','Homeowners submitted no views.','Why include independent scrutiny?','To assess whose views actually shaped the decision.','To guarantee agreement on every issue.','To exclude all open submissions.','conferring legitimacy','giving a decision an appearance of justified authority','counting the total number of letters','requiring unanimous approval','Draft a recommendation for redesigning the consultation. Reconcile openness with representation, consider a risk of targeted outreach, and specify how accountability would be assessed.','Develop a nuanced position with precise concessions. Explain the tension between procedural access and substantive influence, propose a safeguard against selective outreach, and define an observable accountability criterion.')
]
def quote(s): return "'"+s.replace("'","''")+"'"
statements=['-- Additive scenario curriculum: six skills at every CEFR level.\nbegin;']
for row in rows:
 level,title,passage,explanation,gq,gc,gw1,gw2,rq,rc,rw1,rw2,lq,lc,lw1,lw2,word,meaning,mw1,mw2,task,rubric=row
 for skill in ['grammar','vocabulary','reading','listening','writing','speaking']:
  slug=f'{level.lower()}-{skill}-scenario-workshop'
  notes={'grammar':explanation,'vocabulary':f'In this context, {word} means {meaning}. Learn the phrase with its sentence, then use it in a new example. Check that the surrounding words preserve the same meaning.','reading':'Read for the overall situation first, then distinguish stated details from conclusions. Support each answer with a phrase from the passage. '+explanation,'listening':'Use Play example audio to hear browser-generated English speech. Listen once for the main situation and again for the specific detail. The transcript is available for review; synthetic speech is not a recording of a real conversation.','writing':'Plan your response before drafting: situation, supporting detail, and useful next step. Read it again for time references, linking words, and whether it answers every part of the task. '+explanation,'speaking':'Use the optional browser speech-to-text control, or type an outline if it is unavailable. Practise saying your answer aloud. Transcription does not evaluate pronunciation or fluency. '+explanation}[skill]
  statements.append(f'''do $lesson$ declare l uuid; e uuid; begin
 insert into public.lessons(title,slug,description,cefr_level,category,order_index,estimated_minutes,is_published)
 values({quote(title+' · '+skill)},'{slug}',{quote('Practise '+skill+' through a practical scenario with guided feedback.')},'{level}','{skill}',20,15,false) returning id into l;
 insert into public.lesson_sections(lesson_id,title,content,order_index) values(l,'How to approach this task',{quote(notes)},1),(l,'Worked example',{quote(passage)},2);
''')
  if skill in ['writing','speaking']:
   statements.append(f"insert into public.exercises(lesson_id,exercise_type,prompt,rubric,order_index) values(l,'short_response',{quote(task)},{quote(rubric+' This response earns participation credit; it is not automatically marked correct or assigned a proficiency score.')},1);")
  else:
   qs={'grammar':[(gq,gc,gw1,gw2,explanation),(rq,rc,rw1,rw2,'Use the stated details in the scenario.')], 'vocabulary':[(f'What does “{word}” mean in this context?',meaning,mw1,mw2,f'The surrounding context supports the meaning: {meaning}.'),(rq,rc,rw1,rw2,'Check the scenario, rather than relying on an isolated word.')], 'reading':[(rq,rc,rw1,rw2,'The passage states the facts supporting this answer.'),(lq,lc,lw1,lw2,'Distinguish the stated plan or limitation from stronger unsupported claims.')], 'listening':[(lq,lc,lw1,lw2,'Listen again for the relevant detail. '+passage),(rq,rc,rw1,rw2,'The transcript provides this detail. '+passage)]}[skill]
   for i,(prompt,correct,w1,w2,feedback) in enumerate(qs,1):
    kind={'grammar':'fill_blank','reading':'reading_comprehension','listening':'listening'}.get(skill,'multiple_choice')
    statements.append(f"insert into public.exercises(lesson_id,exercise_type,prompt,passage,order_index) values(l,'{kind}',{quote(prompt)},{quote(passage)},{i}) returning id into e;")
    # Vary the correct answer position.
    options=[(w1,False),(correct,True),(w2,False)] if i==1 else [(correct,True),(w2,False),(w1,False)]
    for j,(text,ok) in enumerate(options,1):
     statements.append(f"insert into public.exercise_options(exercise_id,option_text,is_correct,explanation,order_index) values(e,{quote(text)},{str(ok).lower()},{quote(('Correct. ' if ok else 'Review the scenario. ')+feedback)},{j});")
  statements.append('update public.lessons set is_published=true where id=l; end $lesson$;')
statements.append("do $exam$ declare x uuid; q uuid; begin insert into public.exam_sets(title,description,cefr_level,duration_seconds,is_published) values('Academic evidence and decisions','Unofficial TOEFL-style skills practice. Synthetic listening audio; no official score or speech evaluation.','B2',1800,true) returning id into x;")
for i,row in enumerate(rows[3:],1):
 level,title,passage,explanation,gq,gc,gw1,gw2,rq,rc,rw1,rw2,lq,lc,lw1,lw2,word,meaning,mw1,mw2,task,rubric=row
 for j,(category,prompt,correct,w1,w2) in enumerate([('reading',rq,rc,rw1,rw2),('listening',lq,lc,lw1,lw2),('vocabulary',f'In context, what does “{word}” mean?',meaning,mw1,mw2)],1):
  statements.append(f"insert into public.exam_questions(exam_id,category,prompt,passage,is_objective,order_index) values(x,'{category}',{quote(prompt)},{quote(passage)},true,{i*10+j}) returning id into q;")
  for k,(text,ok) in enumerate([(w1,False),(correct,True),(w2,False)],1):
   statements.append(f"insert into public.exam_question_options(question_id,option_text,is_correct,explanation,order_index) values(q,{quote(text)},{str(ok).lower()},{quote('Review the evidence in the passage: '+passage)},{k});")
 statements.append(f"insert into public.exam_questions(exam_id,category,prompt,rubric,is_objective,order_index) values(x,'writing',{quote(task)},{quote(rubric)},false,{i*10+4});")
statements.append('end $exam$;')
statements.append('commit;')
Path('supabase/migrations/20261028000005_scenario_curriculum.sql').write_text('\n'.join(statements)+'\n')
